 "verdict": "THE BRIDGE DEPENDS ON THE PHASE AT FIXED INFLOW, AND THE OUTCOME FOLLOWS IT THERE. At the most crowded inflow value, F_local = 0.0225 with 26 phase classes, the contact ratio spans 0.00555-0.45354 (spread 0.44799, bar 0.05) - so the bridge is not a function of the inflow alone - and the worlds above that value's median ratio fuse 0.8889 more often than those below (Fisher p = 0.0, bar 0.3). Over the population the ratio falls with the inflow (Spearman -0.378 over classes, -0.833 over the nine value means; bar -0.5) and the logistic slope of fusion on the ratio over the 144 worlds is 6.094 (se 1.058, z = 5.76). The mechanism of the flip is therefore a property of the field between the bodies at a given inflow, and the law's boundary condition has to be written per phase, not per inflow. 3 of 4 registered criteria passed."
